hadiths[44]{hadithnumber,text}:
"483","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) sent Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) to Yemen. Then he narrated the entire hadith, in which there is: \Allah Almighty has made Zakat obligatory on their wealth"
"484","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (RA) that Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) wrote this text to Hazrat Anas (RA) regarding the duty of Zakat which the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) had prescribed for the Muslims and which Allah (SWT) ordered to His Messenger: \There are goats for twenty-four camels or less\"""
"485","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Muadh bin Jabal that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him (by appointing an agent) to Yemen and ordered him to receive a one-year-old calf or heifer from every thirty cows and a Musnah (two-toothed cow or ox) from every forty. And take from every adult male a dinar or its equivalent of a piece of cloth (as tribute). (Narrated by all five. The words of the text are Ahmad's and Tirmidhi classifies it as Hasan and points out the disagreement about its reception, and it is said to be Sahih by both Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim.)"
"486","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father (Shuayb) and he from his grandfather (Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Zakat will be collected from the Muslims at their watering places.\"""""
"487","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no zakat (obligation) on a Muslim on his (servant) slave and on his (riding) horse.\"""""
"488","Hazrat Bahz bin Hakeem narrates from his father and he (Hakim) from his (Bahz) grandfather, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For every forty camels that graze in the forest, there is one Bint Lubun (two-year-old female camel) and they will not be separated on their account. A person who pays Zakat with the intention of getting reward, then for him there is reward and reward. And whoever withholds Zakat, We will forcefully collect from him and take half of his wealth (and more). This is one of the duties of our Lord. There is no share in it for the family of Muhammad.''"
"489","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When you have two hundred dirhams and a whole year has passed on them"
"490","Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that Zakat is not obligatory on working oxen. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and Daraqtani. It is Rajah that it is also muquf.)"
"491","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrates from his father and he from his grandfather Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever becomes the guardian of a wealthy orphan"
"492","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Abi Ufa (may Allah be pleased with him) that when people came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with Zakat, he used to pray for them like this. Ya Allah! Have mercy on them.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"493","It was narrated from Hazrat Ali (RA) that Hazrat Abbas (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) whether Zakat can be paid before its due time. So you gave them permission. (Narrated by Tirmidhi and Hakim)."
"494","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is no Zakat on silver less than five ounces.\"" And there is no Zakat on less than five camels. And there is no zakat on dates less than five wasaqs. (The original of the tradition of Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri"
"495","Hazrat Salem bin Abdullah, may God have mercy on him, narrates from his father. He narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: \The land that is irrigated by the sky (rain) and springs"
"496","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Musa Ash'ari and Mu'adh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: \Do not collect zakat on any grain other than barley"
"497","Hazrat Sahl bin Abi Hatmah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us: “When you make an estimate and guess (of the fruits on the trees), then (you can pick their fruit and then) receive the Zakat according to the estimate and leave a third part (of the estimated fruit). If you cannot leave the third part, then leave the fourth part."
"498","Hazrat Uttab bin Usayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us: “Grapes (unripe fruits) should also be assessed in the same way as dates are assessed. And their zakat should be received in the form of raisins.”"
"499","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father (Shuaib) and he (Shuaib) from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr) that a woman came to the service of the Prophet. His daughter was also with him. And the daughter had two gold bracelets in her hand. He asked this woman: \Do you give her Zakat?\"" She said no. He said: \""Do you like that on the Day of Resurrection"
"500","It is narrated from Hazrat Umm Salamah that she used to wear gold anklets. He inquired, O Messenger of Allah! What: Is it Kunz? He said: \When you have paid his zakat"
"501","It was narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to order us to collect Zakat from trading goods. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and its chain of transmission is weak.)"
"502","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \There is Khums (fifth share) in the buried treasure.\"" (Bukhari and Muslim)."""
"503","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates from his father and he from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about a treasure that a man found in a desolate place: “If you find this treasure in an inhabited place, announce it for investigation. And if you found it in an uninhabited place, then it is a fifth part in it and in Raqaz.”"
"504","It was narrated from Hazrat Bilal bin Harith (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) received Zakat from the mines located in Qabul. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud.)"
"505","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) ordered every slave, free, male, female, young and old, to give one saa of dates or one saa as Sadaqah al-Fitr to every Muslim. And it has been ordered that it should be paid before going out for Salah (Eid). (Bukhari and Muslim) In Ibn Udi and Darqutni, it is with a weak chain of transmission: “On this (Eid) day, make them (the poor) free from wandering around the village.”"
"506","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to give one Sa'a (Fitrana) of grains (wheat), dates, barley or raisins. (Bukhari and Muslim) And there is a hadith: \Or he used to take out a saa from the cheese.\"" Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said"
"507","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) prescribed Sadaqah al-Fitr (Al-Fitr) to cleanse the fasting person from lewdness and obscenity and to feed the poor. Whoever pays it before offering the prayer, then it is acceptable, and whoever pays it after the prayer, then it is one of the (common) sadaqahs. (Not Sadaqah al-Fitr.) (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Ibn Majah, and Hakim said it to be Sahih.)"
"508","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah will place seven types of people in His shadow"
"509","It was narrated from Hazrat Uqba bin Aamir (RA) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “Every man will stand in the shadow of his charity until the people are judged.” (Narrated by Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim)."
"510","Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Whoever clothes a naked Muslim, Allah will clothe him with the green clothes of Paradise.” And whoever feeds a hungry Muslim, Allah will feed him with the fruits of Paradise. And the Muslim who gives (water or drink) to a thirsty Muslim, Allah will make him drink from the pure sealed wine of Paradise."
"511","Hazrat Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) that he said: “The upper hand is better than the lower hand. And start (almsgiving) with those whom he supports and takes care of. And the best charity is that which the giver remains rich after giving. Whoever refrains from asking questions, Allah will save him. And the one who shows indifference, Allah will make him indifference.\""512"""
"512","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?"" He said: ""The effort of the one with little means, and begin with those whom you support."" Narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud, and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah, Ibn Hibban, and Al-Hakim."
"513","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Give charity and charity.\"" A man said: O Messenger of Allah! I have one dinar. He said: \""Spend it on your life.\"" He said: \""I have another.\"" He said: \""Spend it on your children.\"" He then said: I have another. He said: \""Spend it on your wife.\"" He then said"
"514","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “A woman who gives charity from the food of her house, provided that her intention is not to spoil the house, then she will surely get the reward and reward for what she gives in charity and her husband will also be rewarded because of what he earns.” And in the same way the treasurer will be rewarded, and the reward of one will not diminish the reward of another.\ (Bukhari and Muslim)"""
"515","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri (RA) that Hazrat Zainab (RA) the wife of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masood (RA) came and said: O Messenger of Allah! You have ordered to give charity today. I have my personal jewelry, I want to give it as charity, but Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) thinks that he and his children are more deserving of giving charity to them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) has said the right thing.\"" Your husband and your children are more deserving of your charity.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"""
"516","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \A man who always asks questions and begs people"
"517","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever asks people for their wealth (not out of necessity but) with the intention of increasing his wealth"
"518","On the authority of Hazrat Zubayr bin Al-Awam, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you holds a rope, then carries a bundle of wood (from the forest) on his back and sells it, so that Allah may protect his honor and dignity, then this is better for him than asking whether people should give it to him or not.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"519","It is narrated from Hazrat Samura bin Jundab, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \To ask a question is like inflicting a wound and scratching"
"520","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Zakah (and Zakat) is not lawful for a rich and wealthy person except for five types of people. 1. Collector of Zakat and Sadaqah. 2. The (wealthy) person who buys charity with his wealth. 3. Indebtedness. 4. One who fights in the way of Allah. 5. Alms was given to a poor person and he gave it as a gift to a rich and wealthy man."""
"521","Hazrat Ubaidullah bin Udi bin Khiyar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that two men narrated to him their incident that they both attended the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (while he was distributing charity). They both asked him for charity. You took a look at them both from top to bottom and found them both powerful. He said: \If you wish"
"522","On the authority of Hazrat Qubaysa bin Makhariq Hilali, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Questioning is permissible only for three people: A person who has taken a guarantee"
"523","On the authority of Hazrat Abdul Muttalib bin Rabi'ah bin Harith, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Undoubtedly"
"524","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Jubayr bin Mut'am (may Allah be pleased with him) that I and Hazrat Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah! You gave the Banu Matla a share of the Khums of Khyber and neglected us, even though we and they are equal in relation to you. (On hearing this) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Banu Matal and Banu Hashim are one and the same thing.” (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"525","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Rafi' that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a man from Banu Makhzoom to collect alms and zakat. He said to Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him, \Come with me"
"526","Hazrat Salim bin Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated from his father (Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would give something to Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would say: Give it to those who are poorer than me. In response to this, he used to say: \Take it\"" then make it your wealth or give it as charity and take whatever wealth comes to you without greed or begging"
